## 🔌 ESP Boards Overview

### ESP32 (Host & Clients)
- **Core:** Dual-core, 240 MHz
- **Wi-Fi:** Built-in 2.4 GHz
- **RAM:** 520 KB
- **ADC:** 12-bit (0-4095) — GPIO 32, 33, 34, 35, 36, 39
- **Use:** Host aur zyada tar clients ke liye. Fast processing aur zyada GPIO pins ki wajah se servo, DHT, aur multiple sensors easily chal jate hain.

### ESP8266 (NodeMCU / Lolin)
- **Core:** Single-core, 80/160 MHz
- **Wi-Fi:** Built-in 2.4 GHz
- **RAM:** 160 KB
- **ADC:** 10-bit (0-1023) — Sirf ek pin (A0), max 1.0V
- **Use:** Sasta aur chhota board. Wahan use hota hai jahan kam sensors ho. Ismein analog sensor lagane ke liye voltage divider zaroori hai.

